{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjXZcjxMNyrcEK7jzxXi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012u64BEAJVpDUtxhXBNqScp","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start of the line, before the repeat sign: a tie or slur comes in from the left edge to a G#4, then three more G#4 16ths and a G#4 8th. That is the end of bar 36: the tied G#4 16th, then G#4 16th ×3 and G#4 8th. The line before starts bar 36 (G#4 8th, rest 8th, G#4 16th, G#4 8th, G#4 16th tied), and this line finishes it. After the double bar with repeat dots comes a lone 8th rest. That is bar 37, the upbeat after the repeat sign. Next bar: 8th rest, then B4 A4 16ths, a slashed grace A4, G#4 8th, G#4 A4 16ths, slurred B4 dotted 8th–D5 16th, D5 8th and 8th rest, with p under it. That is bar 38. The next bar has the same figure, so it is bar 39. Last bar: a slurred F#4 G#4 A4 B4 in 8ths, a slurred A4 G#4, then F#4 16th, F#4 8th, F#4 16th, with cres. under it. That is bar 40, and it closes at the final barline of the line. Nothing contradicts the edition. The only miss is the start: the line begins with the end of bar 36, not with bar 37.","right":false,"insights":"The bars from 38 on were easy to match: the grace-note figure repeats exactly, and the bar 40 scale is distinctive. The program most likely missed the opening because the run of repeated G#4s before the repeat sign looks like a pickup, not the end of bar 36. A clear tie coming in from the line before, or bar numbers on the copy, would have settled where the line starts."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5560,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5560},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti